Kind: ablation
Issue: #659
Takes out: the bound on a byte's wait for another processor's report -- cons_report_wait() waits for as long as the holder holds, as if 0de054a5 had come without CONS_REPORT_CYCLES, so a processor that stops while it holds a report stops every other processor's console with it
Run: --entry 0 600 -smp 4
With: 659-widen-report-held.patch
Expect: widen 659-widen-report-held: that line took ([3-9][0-9]{3}|[1-9][0-9]{4,}) ms
Note: with the bound the line takes the bound, 4e9 TSC cycles, a second or two on the machines here; without it, until the widen's timer lets the holder go, eight seconds.  Three seconds and more is caught

diff --git a/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/ddb/cons.c b/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/ddb/cons.c
index b597a82f..bed0b973 100644
--- a/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/ddb/cons.c
+++ b/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/ddb/cons.c
@@ -577,7 +577,7 @@ static void cons_report_wait(void)
 	epoch = cons_report_epoch;
 	t0 = rdtsc_ordered();
 	while (cons_report_owner == owner && cons_report_epoch == epoch) {
-		if (rdtsc_ordered() - t0 >= CONS_REPORT_CYCLES) {
+		if (0 && rdtsc_ordered() - t0 >= CONS_REPORT_CYCLES) {
 			cons_report_waited_out = epoch;
 			return;
 		}
